Independently review this bounded Plan phase lifecycle repair. Complete physical coordinator and tests follow. On unexpected executor throws, it preserves latest progress, pauses the plan, settles running step callbacks, drains persistence, then saves the authoritative final snapshot. Review and main execution share this mechanism. Completed steps are retained. Duplicate engine fields cannot spend a same-engine retry. Required persistence failures intentionally fail closed. Review errors are not called proven blocking findings. Abort registrations are released in reverse order through compare-owner host callbacks. Review code correctness and test discrimination; report concrete defects with counterexamples. No tools available. Do not approve the full release.
The prior phase review exposed additional bugs and tests now reproduce them: onStepDone is observed via the canonical Plan state transition, callbacks are sealed after return/throw, a child phase signal aborts orphaned work on error without spending the parent fallback grant, cancelled/done terminal states survive later exceptions, and an already aborted review gate pauses without starting review or consuming its budget. Retry state is persisted before being advertised as active. Callback disposal is not passed to the executor. Review these repairs for concrete remaining correctness defects.

